l crisis, influencing regional integration efforts and development policy. Her repeated appointments underscore a consistent, experienced hand in Central American diplomacy.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-25T07:03:30Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30148286785", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Mireya Agüero or Mireya Agüero de Corrales is a Honduran politician who is currently serving as minister for foreign affairs since 2026, and previously from 2013 to 2014.", "newValue": "Mireya Agüero de Corrales, a distinguished Honduran diplomat and politician, has twice served as the Minister of Foreign Affairs for Honduras, first from April 2013 to January 2014 and again commencing in 2026. Her career is defined by her pivotal role in shaping and articulating Honduras's international relations during periods of significant political and economic flux within Central America, establishing her as a central figure in the nation's contemporary diplomatic landscape. She has represented Honduras on global stages, advocating for its foreign policy priorities and engaging with international bodies and key bilateral partners.

